Add one middleware in `app.js` ahead of `express.json()` and `sessionUser`, so the 401s that `sessionUser` returns are logged too. Write the log line on `finish`, when the status code is known and `sessionUser` has already set `req.user`:

```js
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const start = process.hrtime.bigint();
  res.on("finish", () => {
    console.log(JSON.stringify({
      method: req.method,
      path: req.originalUrl,
      status: res.statusCode,
      ms: Number(process.hrtime.bigint() - start) / 1e6,
      userId: req.user && req.user.id,
      accountId: req.user && req.user.accountId,
    }));
  });
  next();
});
```

Leave request bodies out of the log, because the accounts routes accept `billing_email`. Requests killed by the pg crash described earlier never reach `finish`, so they won't appear in these logs.

The remaining choice is where the logs go: JSON on stdout or the logging stack you already run. Which do you use?

